Scenario 1 (Easy → Medium)
Banking System - Account Management

A bank wants to manage different types of accounts.

There are three account types:

Savings Account
Current Account
Fixed Deposit Account

Every account has:

Account Number
Customer Name
Balance

Every account should support

deposit()
withdraw()
displayBalance()

However,

Savings Account
Minimum balance = ₹1000
Withdrawal should fail if balance goes below ₹1000.
Current Account
No minimum balance.
Allows overdraft of ₹10,000.

Example

Balance = ₹5,000

Withdraw = ₹12,000

Allowed.

Remaining balance = -₹7,000

But withdrawing beyond -₹10,000 should fail.

Fixed Deposit Account
Deposit only once during account creation.
Withdrawal is not allowed before maturity.

If withdraw() is called,

Withdrawal not allowed before maturity.
Additional Requirements

Create a main() method that

Creates one object of each account
Deposits money where applicable
Withdraws money
Displays final balances
Constraints

Use these OOP concepts:

✔ Encapsulation

✔ Inheritance

✔ Method Overriding

✔ Runtime Polymorphism

✔ Abstract Class or Interface (your choice)

✔ Constructors

✔ super
